{"title":"2011 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a5003a9ab9c96eee4a9cd7074134b14b1bfb5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + (a + b + c)^2 \\le 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"239\" height=\"19\" />.  Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9f681c05bd7b174a3441b949d98b47dad707070.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{ab + 1}{(a + b)^2} + \\frac{bc + 1}{(b + c)^2} + \\frac{ca + 1}{(c + a)^2} \\ge 3.\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>An integer is assigned to each vertex of a regular pentagon so that the sum of the five integers is 2011. A turn of a solitaire game consists of subtracting an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> from each of the integers at two neighboring vertices and adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c93d829d38f1f73cd97c8fd926e636e968d0c158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2m$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> to the opposite vertex, which is not adjacent to either of the first two vertices. (The amount <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and the vertices chosen can vary from turn to turn.) The game is won at a certain vertex if, after some number of turns, that vertex has the number 2011 and the other four vertices have the number 0. Prove that for any choice of the initial integers, there is exactly one vertex at which the game can be won.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />, which is nonconvex but not self-intersecting, no pair of opposite sides are parallel.  The internal angles satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aab752e6f89be4beabd8bcc01d8945e7cc521c61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = 3 \\angle D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d3d4a5238250a2fe6a474a250089edf92c0097d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C = 3 \\angle F$\" width=\"87\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca4fd9bff73466ba4665e8eeb566baebd92f1cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle E = 3 \\angle B$\" width=\"87\" height=\"12\" />.  Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1df37a7086e510675dc62273ce447c007c68927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = DE$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b706a16d9cf655df740b010afd1a247c72d4f94a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = EF$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f761de814be1cd2bfa531572e3b46330faf1bf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = FA$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />.  Prove that diagonals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc7f4fd0e5897e8ac812a9a562556b8cdd87341f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CF}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> are concurrent.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the assertion that for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, the remainder upon dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c3455b8d6564924f33e1e4ce8b64d2dd90408c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654a7c7010145200d9d8723eda7ce20e98b5723c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is a power of 4.  Either prove the assertion or find (with proof) a counterexample.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a given point inside quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.  Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> are located within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b5666ec397ecdd746334b2ec331bf87a176c544d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle Q_1 BC = \\angle ABP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed33863ca76a9509633a8c1a78f932affb9d1c70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle Q_1 CB = \\angle DCP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"144\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef11ff304b3c7588cca524bf8a8074289a95dda3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle Q_2 AD = \\angle BAP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12b0fafe84581126f5255324b948cbab1c21aae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle Q_2 DA = \\angle CDP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/193f37f10f09601083ae6395c2a4755181bb3944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{Q_1 Q_2} \\parallel \\overline{BA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/09482ff57fd8b4e8398d0494e4536e4c2c5f8157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{Q_1 Q_2} \\parallel \\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a set with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed2fa2a4d1f8c024da24d87119ecb00f4a36888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A| = 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has 225 elements.  Suppose further that there are eleven subsets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/6/e26b63cf52b85e36ddb448caf62ff9fc413bce8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca79d8deb15b4682a49e4040736c18f2725390f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_i | = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e52219c2c651752cdf56cca7f8a20073386e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e802ff1811f123978cf75af969c2af42ded07c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_i \\cap A_j| = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad19b6e98d4264bb67d4dffd7732789e7c0289c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i &lt; j \\le 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" />.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa7684225ea083fac9c9ae39a49e8eab2f31552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A_1 \\cup A_2 \\cup \\dots \\cup A_{11}| \\ge 165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />, and give an example for which equality holds.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO\" title=\"2011 USAMO\">2011 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_USAMO\" title=\"2010 USAMO\">2010 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO\" title=\"2012 USAMO\">2012 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018055043\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 275/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 920/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 64/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7776/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.854      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n100.00%    6.854      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9282:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018055043 and revision id 78107. Render